.TH UDECK-TERMINAL-DEFAULT 1 "2026-11-09" "uDeck 0.2.3"
.SH NAME
udeck-terminal-default \- configure or restore Debian and XDG terminal defaults
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B udeck-terminal-default status
.RI [ --user " USER" ]
.br
.B sudo udeck-terminal-default apply --system
.br
.B sudo udeck-terminal-default restore --system
.br
.B sudo udeck-terminal-default apply --user USER
.br
.B sudo udeck-terminal-default restore --user USER --backup BACKUP.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
Package installation automatically applies system defaults. It registers the
x-terminal-emulator alternative at priority 20 with its manual-page slave,
backs up the previous auto/manual selection and system XDG preferences,
and explicitly selects uDeck Terminal. System mode does not edit user profiles.
Physical acceptance is recorded independently and is not required to apply.
.PP
Explicit user mode also updates the target user's XDG lists and supported
desktop bindings, with a separate recovery manifest printed by apply.
.PP
System restore is also run on package removal. It removes this package's
preferences, keeps subsequent administrator changes and restores the previous
terminal when still available. User restore refuses to overwrite files changed
after apply; keep the backup and reconcile those changes manually.
.SH FILES
.I /var/lib/udeck-terminal/defaults/
contains private, root-owned recovery manifests. Configuration symlinks and
unsupported explicit terminal flags require manual migration before apply.
.PP
.I /var/lib/udeck-terminal/system-defaults.json
records package-managed system defaults and is removed on restoration.
.SH VERIFICATION
Configuration success does not prove launch behavior. Verify the alternative,
xdg-terminal-exec, Gio Terminal=true, keyboard shortcuts and file managers in
both desktop environments. Rehearse restoration before final default selection.
